WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:13.576
Components is your software release library. Use it to prepare a
named version once, then deploy that version to selected devices
or groups. Publishing a release and choosing who receives it are
separate steps.

2
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:24.968
The first time you publish, set up your publisher catalog and
approve the request. The catalog keeps your releases organized
so you can find and reuse them for later deployments.

3
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:36.987
Give the component a recognizable name and the release a version
number. Keep versions distinct so operators can tell which
release was deployed and compare results when troubleshooting.

4
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:53.187
Choose the target operating system and processor architecture,
then attach the software file for that platform. Include the
installation instructions your platform needs. Matching the
platform helps avoid sending a package that the device cannot
run.

5
00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:08.768
Choose Confidential for proprietary software and select an
access policy. That policy controls who can obtain the
decryption keys. This demonstration deliberately uses a public
example, so its uploaded files are readable by anyone.

6
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:23.453
Review the release, upload it to storage, and approve
publication. The recorded file fingerprints let the device
verify that it received the intended content. Wait for
confirmation before treating the version as available.

7
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:10.648
The published version is now in the library. Publishing has not
installed it on any device. Next, choose the devices or group
that should receive it and create a deployment.

